          %h1#contents Contents
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#definition"} Definition
              %li
                %a{:href => "#via_embedding"} Via embedding
              %li
                %a{:href => "#via_exact_structure"} Via exact structure
              %li
                %a{:href => "#properties"} Properties
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#quillengabriel_embedding_theorem"} Quillen-Gabriel embedding theorem
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#relation_to_waldhausen_categories_and_algebraic_ktheory"} Relation to Waldhausen categories and algebraic K-theory
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h2#via_embedding Via embedding
          %p
            A full
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/additive+category"} additive
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subcategory"} subcategory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            is called
            %strong Quillen exact category
            if it is closed under
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extensions"} extensions
            (if in extension
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi j
                    %mi Y
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi p
                    %mi Z
                    %mo →
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0\to X\stackrel{j}\to Y\stackrel{p}\to Z\to 0
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z
            are in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            is in
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A,E)
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            is the class of all short exact sequences in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            which are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+sequence"} exact
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
          %p
            All
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi j
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
            which appear as
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi j
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
            in an exact sequence as above are called
            = succeed "s" do
              %strong inflation
            = succeed "s." do
              %strong admissible monomorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            which appear in an exact sequence as above are called
            = succeed "s" do
              %strong deflation
            = succeed "s." do
              %strong admissible epimorphism
          %h2#via_exact_structure Via exact structure
          %p
            A
            %strong Quillen exact category
            is a pair
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A,E)
            of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/additive+category"} additive category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and a class of sequences
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            called ‘exact’. The following axioms are required for
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A,E)
          %p
            (QE1) The class of ‘exact’ sequences is closed under
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cokernel"} cokernel
            of inflation and the inflation is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel"} kernel
            of the deflation.
          %p
            (QE2) The class of deflations is closed under
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+change"} base change
            by arbitrary maps. The class of inflations is closed under compositions and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobase+change"} cobase change
            by arbitrary maps.
          %p
            (QE3) If a morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %mo →
                  %mi M
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M\to M'
            having a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel"} kernel
            can factor a deflation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                  %mo →
                  %mi M
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N\to M'
            as
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                  %mo →
                  %mi M
                  %mo →
                  %mi M
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N\to M\to M'
            then it is a deflation. If a morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                  %mo →
                  %mi I
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I\to I'
            having a cokernel can factor an inflation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                  %mo →
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I\to J
            as
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                  %mo →
                  %mi I
                  %mo ′
                  %mo →
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I\to I'\to J
            then it is also an inflation.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#quillengabriel_embedding_theorem Quillen-Gabriel embedding theorem
          %p
            For every small exact category in the sense of a pair
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A,E)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\hookrightarrow B
            into an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian category
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            is a class of all sequences which are (short) exact in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
          %h3#relation_to_waldhausen_categories_and_algebraic_ktheory Relation to Waldhausen categories and algebraic K-theory
          %p
            Every Quillen exact category can be made into a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Waldhausen+category"} Waldhausen category
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+K-theory"} algebraic K-theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen%27s+Q-construction"} Quillen's Q-construction
            and an exact category agrees with the K-theory spectrum based on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Waldhausen+S-construction"} Waldhausen S-construction
            of the K-theory spectrum from its associated
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Waldhausen+category"} Waldhausen category
          %h2#references References
          %p Quillen introduced exact categories in above sense in the article
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Quillen"}> Daniel Quillen
              , “Higher algebraic K-theory”, in Higher K-theories, pp. 85–147, Proc. Seattle 1972, Lec. Notes Math. 341, Springer 1973.
          %p
            A nonadditive generalization of exact categories has been introduced by Dyckerhoff and Kapranov and named a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proto-exact+category"} proto-exact category
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Rosenberg"} Alexander Rosenberg
            %a{:href => "http://www.mpim-bonn.mpg.de/preprints/send?bid=3623"} introduced
            one sided generalizations of Quillen exact categories: right ‘exact’ categories involving deflations, and left ‘exact’ categories involving inflations. One of the motivations an alternative definition of higher K-theory of (right exact) categories not involving spectra. In this setup the K-theory is an example of a derived functor in nonabelian homological algebra utilizing roughly the left ‘exact’ structure on the category of essentially small right ‘exact’ categories. It is not known if this K-theory when restricted to the category of essentially small Quillen exact categories agrees with Quillen K-theory. But it has the standard properties of Quillen K-theory (devissage, exactness and so on).
          %p
            The one-sided generalization inspired by ideas introduced by Keller and Vossieck in the build up of the theory of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/suspended+category"} suspended categories
          %p
            A right ‘exact’ category is a category with an initial object and a Grothendieck pretopology consisting of single maps which are
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+epimorphism"} strict epimorphism
            = succeed "." do
              %em deflations
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/satellite"} satellites
          %ul
            %li
              Dmitry Kaledin, Wendy Lowen,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Cohomology of exact categories and (non-)additive sheaves
              %strong 272
              (2015) 652–698
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1102.5756"} arXiv:1102.5756
